{
  "$defs": {
    "BlobRef": {
      "description": "A content-addressed object reference (ID-4).",
      "properties": {
        "bytes": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Bytes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "media_type": {
          "title": "Media Type",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "part_count": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Part Count"
        },
        "sha256": {
          "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$",
          "title": "Sha256",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "sha256",
        "bytes",
        "media_type"
      ],
      "title": "BlobRef",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EarlyStopping": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "When to stop boosting, and against what (FR-MODEL-30).\n\n**There is no `train` value**, and that is the requirement rather than an oversight:\na stopping rule read off the data being fitted stops when the model has finished\nmemorising. Refusing it by construction means no validator can be relaxed into\nallowing it.",
      "properties": {
        "cv_folds": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 2,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Cv Folds"
        },
        "metric": {
          "title": "Metric",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "on": {
          "enum": [
            "holdout",
            "cv"
          ],
          "title": "On",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "rounds": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Rounds",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "on",
        "metric",
        "rounds"
      ],
      "title": "EarlyStopping",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GbmFunctionRef": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A builtin objective or eval metric by name, or an approved artifact by reference.\n\nOne shape for both because FR-MODEL-26 and FR-MODEL-45 declare the same choice twice —\na builtin the backend already implements, or a Custom Objective / Custom Metric that\ncarries its own approval status (R4). Two classes with identical fields would be a\nshape defined twice.",
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "enum": [
            "builtin",
            "custom"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "name": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Name"
        },
        "ref": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ref"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "kind"
      ],
      "title": "GbmFunctionRef",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GbmSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "`02` §4.4's common block plus the gradient-boosting arm (FR-MODEL-25).\n\n**One contract, two backends.** `model_type` is the backend — §4.4 also gave this arm a\n`backend` field carrying the same two strings, and two fields holding one fact can\ndisagree with nothing downstream able to say which to believe. Backend-specific tuning\nlives in `backend_params`, which is what keeps the contract from forking.\n\n**The offset is declared once.** §4.4 also gave this arm a `base_margin` block of the\nsame shape as the common `offset`. FR-MODEL-27 says the platform *constructs*\n`base_margin` from the declared offset, so a second declaration is a second source of\ntruth for the one number the fit silently depends on. What was actually constructed is\nrecorded on the fit result, where FR-MODEL-71 can assert it at load time.\n\nBoth corrections are recorded in `02` §4.4, dated 2026-08-17.",
      "properties": {
        "backend_params": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Backend Params",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "categorical_handling": {
          "enum": [
            "native",
            "factor_encoding"
          ],
          "title": "Categorical Handling",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "dataset_version_id": {
          "format": "uuid",
          "title": "Dataset Version Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "early_stopping": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/EarlyStopping"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "eval_metrics": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/GbmFunctionRef"
          },
          "title": "Eval Metrics",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "factors": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Factors",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "hyperparameters": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "number"
              }
            ]
          },
          "title": "Hyperparameters",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "interaction_constraints": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "type": "array"
          },
          "title": "Interaction Constraints",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "interval_for": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/IntervalFor"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "loss_treatment": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/LossTreatment",
          "default": {
            "cap_minor": null,
            "evidence_blob": null,
            "kind": "none",
            "restoration_loading": null
          }
        },
        "model_family_slug": {
          "title": "Model Family Slug",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model_type": {
          "enum": [
            "xgboost",
            "lightgbm"
          ],
          "title": "Model Type",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "monotone_constraints": {
          "default": "derived_from_factors",
          "enum": [
            "derived_from_factors",
            "none"
          ],
          "title": "Monotone Constraints",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "objective": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/GbmFunctionRef"
        },
        "offset": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/OffsetSpec",
          "default": {
            "column": null,
            "kind": "none",
            "model_ref": null
          }
        },
        "offset_acknowledgement": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Offset Acknowledgement"
        },
        "peril": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Peril"
        },
        "response": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ResponseKind"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "response_column": {
          "title": "Response Column",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "seed": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Seed",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "split_ref": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/SplitRef"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "weight": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/WeightSpec",
          "default": {
            "column": null,
            "kind": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "model_family_slug",
        "dataset_version_id",
        "response_column",
        "model_type",
        "objective",
        "categorical_handling"
      ],
      "title": "GbmSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GlmCvSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "FR-MODEL-20/FR-MODEL-53: the cross-validated penalty path `GlmSpec.cv` carries when\n`select_by == \"cv\"`.\n\n`seed` is **not** duplicated here: the seed that makes fold assignment reproducible is\n`ModelSpecCommon.seed` — the one seed the spec already carries and already versions\ninto `spec_hash`. A second seed field on this nested block would let the two disagree,\nwhich is the shape-defined-twice trap `CLAUDE.md` §2 names.",
      "properties": {
        "alphas": {
          "default": [
            0.0,
            0.001,
            0.01,
            0.1,
            1.0
          ],
          "items": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "title": "Alphas",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "folds": {
          "default": 5,
          "minimum": 2,
          "title": "Folds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "key_column": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Key Column"
        },
        "method": {
          "default": "random",
          "enum": [
            "random",
            "temporal",
            "grouped_by_key"
          ],
          "title": "Method",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "time_column": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Time Column"
        }
      },
      "title": "GlmCvSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GlmSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "`02` §4.4's common block plus the `glm` arm.\n\nThe spec is what `spec_hash` is taken over, so every field here changes the identity of\nthe model. That is why `loss_treatment` belongs in the spec rather than beside it, and\nwhy two models differing only in a cap must not collide (FR-MODEL-66).",
      "properties": {
        "alpha": {
          "default": 0.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Alpha",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "approximates_model_id": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "format": "uuid",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Approximates Model Id"
        },
        "cv": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/GlmCvSpec"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "dataset_version_id": {
          "format": "uuid",
          "title": "Dataset Version Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "factors": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Factors",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "family": {
          "default": "poisson",
          "enum": [
            "poisson",
            "negative_binomial",
            "gamma",
            "inverse_gaussian",
            "tweedie",
            "binomial",
            "gaussian"
          ],
          "title": "Family",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "family_params": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "title": "Family Params",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "l1_ratio": {
          "default": 0.0,
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "L1 Ratio",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "link": {
          "default": "log",
          "enum": [
            "log",
            "logit",
            "identity",
            "inverse"
          ],
          "title": "Link",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "loss_treatment": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/LossTreatment",
          "default": {
            "cap_minor": null,
            "evidence_blob": null,
            "kind": "none",
            "restoration_loading": null
          }
        },
        "max_iter": {
          "default": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Iter",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "model_family_slug": {
          "title": "Model Family Slug",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model_type": {
          "const": "glm",
          "default": "glm",
          "title": "Model Type",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "offset": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/OffsetSpec",
          "default": {
            "column": null,
            "kind": "none",
            "model_ref": null
          }
        },
        "peril": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Peril"
        },
        "response": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ResponseKind"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "response_column": {
          "title": "Response Column",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "seed": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Seed",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "select_by": {
          "default": "fixed",
          "enum": [
            "fixed",
            "cv"
          ],
          "title": "Select By",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "split_ref": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/SplitRef"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "tolerance": {
          "default": 1e-08,
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Tolerance",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "tweedie": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TweediePowerSpec"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "weight": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/WeightSpec",
          "default": {
            "column": null,
            "kind": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "model_family_slug",
        "dataset_version_id",
        "response_column"
      ],
      "title": "GlmSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "IntervalFor": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "This model is one side of another model's prediction interval (FR-MODEL-78).\n\n**On the spec, so it joins `spec_hash`** (FR-MODEL-100). FR-MODEL-96 set the precedent\nfor a Model that exists relative to another Model — `approximates_model_id` on the\napproximating Model's spec — and the reason is the same one: the pairing is part of\nwhat this model *is*. Two bounds identical but for the central model they bound would\notherwise share a digest, and FR-MODEL-66 would hand the second caller the first\ncaller's model: an interval around a model nobody fitted, rendering identically to a\ncorrect one.\n\nThe central model is named by **id and version**. The id is what the lookup uses; the\nversion is what a human reads in a review, where `motor-ad-frequency@7` is recognisable\nand a UUID is not — the same argument `Prediction` carries for holding both.",
      "properties": {
        "alpha": {
          "exclusiveMaximum": 1.0,
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Alpha",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "model_id": {
          "format": "uuid",
          "title": "Model Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model_version": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Model Version",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "model_id",
        "model_version",
        "alpha"
      ],
      "title": "IntervalFor",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "LossTreatment": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "How large losses are treated **as the model is fitted** (FR-MODEL-73).\n\nA modelling decision, not a property of the data: `01` VR-ACT-10 flags large losses and\nnever removes them, so one validated Dataset Version serves many capping assumptions\nwithout re-ingestion. That is only true while the assumption lives here, inside the\nspec — and therefore inside `spec_hash`, so two models differing only in their cap are\ntwo models rather than a collision (FR-MODEL-66).\n\n`cap_minor` is **integer minor units** (`CLAUDE.md` §7). A cap is a money threshold\ncompared against a money column, and a float one compares unequal to itself at the\nboundary — which decides whether the largest claim in the book was capped.",
      "properties": {
        "cap_minor": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Cap Minor"
        },
        "evidence_blob": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/BlobRef"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "kind": {
          "default": "none",
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "capped",
            "spliced",
            "excess"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "restoration_loading": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Restoration Loading"
        }
      },
      "title": "LossTreatment",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "OffsetSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "`02` §4.4. `log_column` is the frequency default: `offset = log(exposure)`.",
      "properties": {
        "column": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Column"
        },
        "kind": {
          "default": "none",
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "log_column",
            "column",
            "model"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model_ref": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Model Ref"
        }
      },
      "title": "OffsetSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResponseKind": {
      "description": "What a Model Spec is modelling, as distinct from which column holds it.\n\n`02` §4.4 declared `response` beside `response_column` from Phase 0 and nothing was\nbuilt to it, because nothing needed it: the fitting path reads the column, and the\nfamily says what the numbers mean. FR-MODEL-44 needs it — an objective declares the\nresponses it applies to, and a column name cannot be checked against that list. So the\nfield goes live here, under FR-MODEL-87's staging rule, with the slice that populates\nit.\n\nThe first three are FR-MODEL-44's own examples. `conversion` and `retention` are\n`04-optimisation.md`'s demand-model responses, and are here because `focal_binomial`\n(§4.5) exists for exactly them — a catalogue entry whose applicability could not be\nwritten would be a catalogue entry nothing could use.",
      "enum": [
        "claim_count",
        "claim_severity",
        "burning_cost",
        "conversion",
        "retention"
      ],
      "title": "ResponseKind",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "SplitRef": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The named split a model was fitted and judged on (`02` §4.4, `01` FR-DATA-36).\n\nA *reference*, not a description. FR-DATA-36 records the split on the **parent**\nversion precisely so that \"trained on the same split\" is one artifact two models cite,\nrather than two derivations that were believed to match. Naming the part versions\ndirectly here would reintroduce the belief.\n\n`train_part` and `holdout_part` are keys into the split's `parts` map; that they name\ntwo *different* parts is checked here, because a model whose holdout is its training\nset reports a flawless fit and no diagnostic downstream can tell.",
      "properties": {
        "holdout_part": {
          "default": "test",
          "title": "Holdout Part",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "split_artifact_id": {
          "format": "uuid",
          "title": "Split Artifact Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "train_part": {
          "default": "train",
          "title": "Train Part",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "split_artifact_id"
      ],
      "title": "SplitRef",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TweediePowerSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "FR-MODEL-22: the grid over which the Tweedie power `p` is estimated by profile\nlikelihood, and the boundary of that estimate. `GlmSpec.tweedie` being set is the\nspec's request for estimation; the estimated value and its uncertainty are fit-time\nfacts and ride on `GlmFitResult.tweedie` — never a constant baked into the spec.\n\nA scan, not a choice: one point would be a fixed fit, and a maximum at the edge of\nthe scan is refused at fit time (`GLM_TWEEDIE_POWER_GRID_EDGE`) because it reports\nthe scan's boundary as the answer.",
      "properties": {
        "p_grid": {
          "default": [
            1.05,
            1.15,
            1.25,
            1.35,
            1.45,
            1.55,
            1.65,
            1.75,
            1.85,
            1.95
          ],
          "items": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "title": "P Grid",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "TweediePowerSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "WeightSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Severity weights by claim count, burning cost by exposure (FR-MODEL-19).",
      "properties": {
        "column": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Column"
        },
        "kind": {
          "default": "none",
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "column"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "WeightSpec",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "discriminator": {
    "mapping": {
      "glm": "#/$defs/GlmSpec",
      "lightgbm": "#/$defs/GbmSpec",
      "xgboost": "#/$defs/GbmSpec"
    },
    "propertyName": "model_type"
  },
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/GlmSpec"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/GbmSpec"
    }
  ]
}
